1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Cessio is an auditable receivables market built on BOT Chain Mainnet.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The Overview shows the current market, contract evidence, and settlement state.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Receivables are tied to real compute and digital-service invoices.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:35,000
The on-chain evidence panel reads from the deployed Cessio contracts.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The originator opens Create invoice and enters the invoice details.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Delivery evidence confidence is included in the underwriting request.

7
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Cessio evaluates the invoice and returns approval status, risk, and funding capacity.

8
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The approved invoice can now be registered on BOT Chain Mainnet.

9
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:25,000
The wallet signs registration; Cessio never takes custody of user funds.

10
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:35,000
After registration, the app moves to Market and refreshes the listing automatically.

11
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:45,000
The Market shows the invoice target, risk, term, and funding progress.

12
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:55,000
An investor opens the receivable and chooses a partial or full USDT amount.

13
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Funding requires explicit USDT approval followed by a separate confirmation.

14
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Once confirmed, the funding activity is recorded against the connected wallet.

15
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Portfolio brings together the wallet, USDT balance, receipt state, and funding history.

16
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:35,000
The Swap / Bridge tab prepares capital for settlement without Cessio holding user funds.

17
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,269
BDEX provides the swap rail into BOT Chain USDT.
